1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:08,000
Saakshi: proof, not just photos
Anyone can post a clean-up photo. How does a funder know it's real?

2
00:00:08,400 --> 00:00:13,650
Saakshi reads each photo: where, when, what is in it, and its fingerprint.

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:23,650
Chaos to order
The demo archive: Wikimedia Commons photos, sorted onto the map by place and project.

4
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:32,650
The library: every photo on the map, with its band. Search with plain chips.

5
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:40,650
Open any photo and take it apart into its evidence layers.

6
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:46,500
The catch
Four fakes are planted in the archive.

7
00:00:46,800 --> 00:00:53,650
Each is flagged by a fixed rule, with its reason. The fingerprint shows the reused photo.

8
00:00:54,400 --> 00:01:00,650
Flagged photos go to a reviewer: a note, then a decision on the record.

9
00:01:01,400 --> 00:01:09,650
Rules decide, not the model: the same published weights for every photo.

10
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:18,650
Proof to story
Before and after, the litter mask counts the pixels.

11
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:27,650
The project overview: every count is a database total, threaded to its photos.

12
00:01:28,400 --> 00:01:37,650
Every number has a thread to the photos behind it.

13
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:47,650
The public report: click a number, see its photos.

14
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:56,650
Each photo's evidence page: its layers, its ledger, and a history chain anyone can check.

15
00:01:57,400 --> 00:02:05,650
Studio: the report and posts for the campaign, faces blurred.

16
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:13,650
Can't un-blur
Edit a public link to remove the blur and the server refuses it: signed transformations.

17
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:18,600
It keeps watching
At the spot, the phone shows its location fix and the spot's ring.

18
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,650
Simulated camera
The camera here is simulated with an archive photo, so Saakshi sends it to review: the identical file was already submitted.

19
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:34,650
Operator rehearsal
The check-in lands on the Witness Wall with its score.

20
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:42,650
The spot page: its litter trend, measured photo by photo, and where check-ins land.

21
00:02:43,400 --> 00:02:49,650
One A4 poster per spot. Built for Swachhata Hi Seva drives and the funders who back them.
